    content: "When someone is selling an asset with a million dollars or more in gains, the worst thing they can do is guess.\n\nYet that's exactly what happens. People Google \"how to handle capital gains,\" piece together half-answers, and lock in a structure they can't undo, all before they've talked to anyone who does this for a living.\n\nSo we built our front door differently.\n\nThe first conversation with Q-1031 is a free capital-gains strategy consultation. No pitch deck, no pressure. We look at three things:\n\nWhat you're selling.\nWhen you're selling it.\nWhat you want the money to do next.\n\nFrom there, the honest answer might be a 1031 exchange. It might be a 537 Installment Sale Trust. Sometimes it's a combination, and occasionally it's \"here's why you don't need us for this part.\"\n\nThe point of the triage isn't to sell you a product. It's to make sure the structure fits the sale before the sale is final, because afterward your options shrink fast.\n\nThinking about a major sale this year? Start with the free conversation at q-1031.com. Worst case, you walk away better informed.\n\nEducational only, not tax, legal, or investment advice. Consult your own advisors. Provided by Q-1031.",
