    content: "Let's settle a question I get constantly, in the simplest way I can.\n\n1031 exchange or 537 Installment Sale Trust? Here's the quick read.\n\nChoose a 1031 exchange when:\n\nYou're selling investment or business-use real estate.\nYou WANT to stay in real estate and buy a replacement property.\nYou can hit the 45-day and 180-day deadlines.\n\nConsider a 537 IST when:\n\nThe asset isn't 1031-eligible (primary residence, business, crypto, concentrated stock).\nYou want OUT of the asset class, not back into real estate.\nYou'd rather receive payments over time than rush into a replacement deal.\n\nThe oversimplified version: a 1031 keeps you in the game with a new property. A 537 IST lets you exit and defer the tax across years instead of paying it all at once.\n\nPlenty of situations call for one clearly. Some call for a combination. A few call for neither, and a good advisor will tell you that too.\n\nQuick gut check: if you sold a major asset tomorrow, would you want to reinvest into more real estate, or step out entirely? Your answer is the first fork in the road.\n\nTell me which camp you're in below.\n\nEducational only, not tax, legal, or investment advice. Consult your own advisors. Provided by Q-1031.",
