    content: "If you're sitting on a large crypto position or a pile of concentrated stock, you already know the dilemma.\n\nSell, and a massive capital gains bill lands in a single year. Hold, and your entire net worth rides on one volatile asset you keep meaning to diversify out of.\n\nMost people freeze between those two doors. Understandably.\n\nWhat rarely comes up is that capital-gains deferral isn't only a real estate tool.\n\nThe 537 Installment Sale Trust works on a range of appreciated assets, which can include crypto and concentrated equity positions. You sell into an irrevocable trust, take payments over time, and defer the capital gains tax so it's paid as those installments arrive rather than all at once.\n\nThat does two things at the same time. It defers the tax across years instead of detonating it in one year, and it lets you step out of a single concentrated position without the up-front tax acting as a wall.\n\nThis isn't a loophole, and it isn't a sure thing. It's a deliberate structure, and whether it fits depends on the asset, your timeline, and how the sale is built. All investing carries risk, including possible loss of principal.\n\nBut if you've been stuck between \"sell and get crushed by taxes\" and \"hold and stay exposed,\" there may be a third option worth understanding.\n\nWhich problem describes you better: the tax hit, or the concentration risk? Curious where people land.\n\nEducational only, not tax, legal, or investment advice. Consult your own advisors. Provided by Q-1031.",
