    author: { name: 'Q-1031 Exchange Solutions', handle: 'q1031exchange', avatar: '/avatars/q-1031.svg', verified: false },
    content: "Two deadlines. No extensions. Miss one and the whole exchange can unwind. ⏱️\n\nWhen you sell investment real estate and want to defer capital gains tax through a 1031 exchange, the IRS starts two clocks the day you close:\n\n📍 Day 45 — you must identify your replacement property in writing.\n📍 Day 180 — you must close on it.\n\nWeekends and holidays don't pause the count. The clocks generally run concurrently, not back-to-back. And you can't touch the sale proceeds yourself — they sit with a Qualified Intermediary the entire time.\n\nMany blown exchanges aren't blown on day 180. They can be lost on day 1, because nobody set up the QI before closing.\n\nThis is general education, not tax, legal, or investment advice — talk to your own advisors about your situation.\n\nSave this before your next closing. Then DM us \"1031\" to map your timeline with a free strategy call. 📌",
