    title: "Buy First, Sell Later: The Reverse 1031",
    pillar: "A",
    pillarLabel: "1031 Education",
    scheduledISO: "2026-06-23T11:00:00",
    hashtags: "#Reverse1031 #1031Exchange #CapitalGainsDeferral #RealEstateInvesting #InvestmentProperty #QualifiedIntermediary #1031ExchangeTips #RealEstateStrategy #PropertyInvestor #TaxStrategy #RealEstateWealth #NationwideServices",
    visualDescription: "6-slide carousel. Slide 1 (hook): two houses with a curved 'reverse' arrow swapping order, 'Buy first, sell later?' Slide 2: 'Standard 1031: sell → then race to buy in 180 days.' Slide 3: 'Reverse 1031: BUY first → then sell. Deferral intact.' Slide 4: 'Why? So you don't overpay or miss the window in a hot market.' Slide 5: 'The catch: an EAT holds the new property until your old one sells.' Slide 6 (CTA): 'Move when the deal appears, not when the calendar says' + DM REVERSE, disclaimer.",
    type: "Carousel",
    theme: 'light',
    author: { name: 'Q-1031 Exchange Solutions', handle: 'q1031exchange', avatar: '/avatars/q-1031.svg', verified: false },
    content: "Found the perfect replacement property — but you haven't sold yours yet? You may not be stuck. 🔄\n\nMany investors think a 1031 means sell first, then scramble to buy inside 180 days. In a hot market, that can lead to overpaying or missing the window.\n\nThe reverse 1031 flips the order: you acquire the replacement property FIRST, then sell the relinquished one — and may still keep your capital gains deferral.\n\nThe catch? You generally can't hold both properties in your own name during the exchange. An Exchange Accommodation Titleholder (EAT) parks the new property until your old one sells. It's more involved than a standard forward exchange, but it can let you move when the right deal appears instead of when the calendar says so.\n\nGeneral education, not tax, legal, or investment advice — loop in your own advisors.\n\nEyeing a property before you've sold? DM \"REVERSE\" and let's talk structure. 🏘️",
    metrics: { likes: 139, comments: 21, reposts: 3 },
    images: [],
    privacy: 'public',
