    content: "The toilet's overflowing. It's 3 AM. And you're 64. 🚽😴\n\nYou built real wealth in those rental units — maybe $5M to $20M of it. But the tenants, the turnover, the midnight calls? You're done. The problem: sell, and a sizable capital gains bill can be waiting after decades of appreciation and depreciation recapture.\n\nYou don't have to choose between burnout and a tax hit.\n\nA 1031 exchange can roll you out of hands-on rentals and into something more passive while deferring the gain. And for the portion a 1031 can't cover, the 537 Installment Sale Trust may defer that tax across a period of years.\n\nThe right mix depends on you. This is education, not tax, legal, or investment advice — your own advisors should weigh in.\n\nReady to step back from fixing toilets? Visit q-1031.com for a free strategy session. 🏖️",
