    visualDescription: "6-slide carousel. Slide 1 (hook): icons of a storefront, a delivery truck, a stock chart, and a coin, headline 'A 1031 can't touch these.' Slide 2: 'So do you just eat the full tax in year one? Not necessarily.' Slide 3: 'Meet the 537 Installment Sale Trust (IRC §453).' Slide 4: note-to-trust diagram, 'Sell to an irrevocable trust via installment note.' Slide 5: 'Defer the gain. Pay tax as installments over a period of years.' Slide 6 (CTA): 'Best structured BEFORE you sign' + send a message, disclaimer at bottom.",
    type: "Carousel",
    theme: 'light',
    author: { name: 'Q-1031 Exchange Solutions', handle: 'q1031exchange', avatar: '/avatars/q-1031.svg', verified: false },
    content: "$2M business sale. Or a crypto position that climbed dramatically. Same painful question: how much walks out the door in tax? 💸\n\nWhen you sell a business, a FedEx route, a concentrated stock position, or a large crypto holding, a 1031 can't help — it's real-estate-only. So sellers often assume they're stuck paying the full capital gains tax the year they sell.\n\nThe 537 Installment Sale Trust (IRC §453) offers another path. You may be able to structure the sale as an installment note to an irrevocable trust, defer the gain, and pay the tax as installments over a period of years — with the goal of keeping more principal working instead of writing one giant check.\n\nFor business sellers, structuring it well before closing matters most. It's best engaged early, not the week you sign.\n\nGeneral education, not tax, legal, or investment advice. Consult your own advisors.\n\nPlanning an exit in the next 12–24 months? Send a message to start the conversation. 🤝",
